From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0168] sweet: bilinear copy reads each source row once into a cached line buffer

Boot 0175b: with sweetfb_filter=1 the copy of 720x1600 -> 1080x2400 takes 29 ms a frame on
3 processors (nearest ~4.6 ms). The source surfaces are GPU-pool memory mapped
kIOMapWriteCombineCache (Normal non-cacheable), so every source load is uncached, and 0167
does 4 scattered 32-bit uncached loads per panel pixel. Now each copier (the caller of copy()
and each helper) has its own cached line buffer of two source rows (9000 bytes, IOMalloc'd once);
a band loads each source row it needs once, with one sequential memcpy, into a slot tagged with
its row, and blends from the slots. The band's cache invalidate and scan wait stay before any
row is loaded; the panel is still written once per pixel, in order, never read. No buffer (an
allocation failed): the 0167 direct reads. Nearest and 1:1 paths unchanged.

Not compiled locally; CI is the compiler.
